REPL.TOKEN
*14
$7
summary
$159
kevy extension: mint a read-your-writes token — per-shard [generation, offset] pairs (a primary reports its live feed tail; a replica its applied positions).
$5
since
$5
3.0.0
$5
group
$11
replication
$6
syntax
$10
REPL.TOKEN
$10
complexity
$48
O(S) — one (generation, offset) pair per shard
$6
compat
$129
kevy-only: the read-your-writes token; the nearest Redis concept is master_repl_offset, which is not a resumable per-shard cursor
$5
flags
*2
$8
readonly
$9
extension
$9
REPL.WAIT
*14
$7
summary
$274
kevy extension: on a replica, block until every shard has applied the given REPL.TOKEN (then reads are read-your-writes); +OK on success, -MISDIRECTED writer is <primary> on timeout or generation mismatch. Default TIMEOUT 1000 ms, hard cap 60 s. On a primary: immediate +OK.
$5
since
$5
3.0.0
$5
group
$11
replication
$6
syntax
$60
REPL.WAIT gen offset [gen offset ...] [TIMEOUT milliseconds]
$10
complexity
$134
O(S) — a barrier, not a keyspace op; the wall-clock cost is the replication lag, bounded by TIMEOUT (default 1s, hard-capped at 60s)
$6
compat
$133
kevy-only: waits until a (generation, offset) token has been applied, which is what makes read-your-writes possible across a failover
$5
