IDX.COUNT
*14
$7
summary
$59
Count index entries matching a range or equality predicate.
$5
since
$5
3.0.0
$5
group
$5
index
$6
syntax
$39
IDX.COUNT name RANGE min max | EQ value
$10
complexity
$109
O(log N + matched) per shard — NOT an O(1) counter and not a B-tree rank query; it counts the matched range
$6
compat
$46
kevy-only: nearest is FT.SEARCH with LIMIT 0 0
$5
flags
*2
$8
readonly
$9
extension
$10
IDX.CREATE
*14
$7
summary
$82
Declare a secondary index over a key prefix (catalog mutation, sidecar-persisted).
$5
since
$5
3.0.0
$5
group
$5
index
$6
syntax
$178
IDX.CREATE name ON PREFIX prefix FIELD field TYPE i64|f64|str|vector KIND range|unique|text|ann|agg [MAXMEM bytes] [DIM dim] [DISTANCE cosine|l2|ip] [M m] [EF ef] [GROUPBY field]
$10
complexity
$240
O(1) at the call; the build is asynchronous — each shard snapshots its matching keys (O(keys on that shard)) then backfills 2048 rows per tick. Per-row build cost: range/unique O(log N), text O(tokens), vector O(ef_construction * M * dim)
$6
compat
$349
kevy-only: nearest is RediSearch FT.CREATE — comparable declarative index-on-prefix, but RediSearch is a module (`redisearch.so`, auto-loaded in Redis 8 and running in the server's own process, not a separate index server) whose index is maintained asynchronously; kevy's catalog is part of the engine and the index is maintained in the write hook
$5
