IDX.VERIFY
*14
$7
summary
$279
Verify an index. Scalar kinds re-read every held entry against its row and report entries/bytes/coerce_failures/duplicates/drift/checked/missing (both audit directions); agg/text/ann answer their own sizing vocabulary (rows|docs|vectors, bytes, ...) and carry no row-keyed audit.
$5
since
$5
3.0.0
$5
group
$5
index
$6
syntax
$15
IDX.VERIFY name
$10
complexity
$159
O(N) per shard — every held entry is re-read against its row and re-coerced, which is the point: it makes index drift falsifiable rather than merely asserted
$6
compat
$118
kevy-only: no Redis analogue — RediSearch's index is asynchronously maintained and offers no consistency-verify verb
$5
